---
// p95 of three runs per endpoint from the p09_burst.py capture (200 requests, 5 at a time,
// bound 70 ms). Bars are scaled to one axis: 0..110 ms over 560 px.
const W = 900, H = 400;
const runs = [
  { key: 'eager', en: '/eager', vi: '/eager', p95: [37.6, 36.7, 32.5], note: { en: 'selectinload: 2 queries per request', vi: 'selectinload: 2 query mỗi request' } },
  { key: 'lazy', en: '/lazy', vi: '/lazy', p95: [84.6, 88.3, 86.8], note: { en: 'N+1: 101 queries per request', vi: 'N+1: 101 query mỗi request' } },
];
const X0 = 160, SCALE = 560 / 110;
const bound = X0 + 70 * SCALE;
---
<figure class="bep9f">
  <div class="bep9f-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Bars of p95 latency in milliseconds, three runs per endpoint. The eager endpoint measured 37.6, 36.7 and 32.5, all under the 70 millisecond bound. The lazy endpoint measured 84.6, 88.3 and 86.8, all over the bound.">
    <text x="20" y="26" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>p95 per run, 200 requests, 5 at a time (ms)</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>p95 mỗi lượt, 200 request, 5 request cùng lúc (ms)</tspan>
    </text>
    {runs.map((r, gi) => (
      <g>
        <text x="20" y={80 + gi * 150} class="nm">{r.en}</text>
        <text x="20" y={100 + gi * 150} class="bs">
          <tspan data-lang-en>{r.note.en}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{r.note.vi}</tspan>
        </text>
        {r.p95.map((v, i) => (
          <g>
            <rect x={X0} y={50 + gi * 150 + i * 32} width={v * SCALE} height="22" rx="4" class={r.key === 'lazy' ? 'bar red' : 'bar'} />
            <text x={X0 + v * SCALE + 8} y={66 + gi * 150 + i * 32} class="val">{v.toFixed(1)}</text>
          </g>
        ))}
      </g>
    ))}
    <line x1={bound} y1="40" x2={bound} y2="340" class="bound" />
    <text x={bound} y="360" text-anchor="middle" class="bs">
      <tspan data-lang-en>bound: 70 ms</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>ngưỡng: 70 ms</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="20" y="386" class="bs">
      <tspan data-lang-en>one laptop running the client, the server and other jobs (load average 11.87 right after): it shows which side of the bound, not capacity</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>một laptop vừa chạy client, server và việc khác (load average 11.87 ngay sau đó): chỉ cho biết nằm bên nào của ngưỡng, không đo được sức chịu tải</tspan>
    </text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>The bound does not need to be precise. It needs to sit between two behaviours that are clearly different, so a regression flips the exit code and noise does not.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Ngưỡng không cần chính xác. Nó chỉ cần nằm giữa hai hành vi khác nhau rõ rệt, để một lần hồi quy làm đổi exit code còn nhiễu thì không.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bep9f { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .bep9f-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bep9f svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 700px; height: auto; }
  .bep9f text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bep9f .h { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 15px; }
  .bep9f .nm { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 16px; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .bep9f .val { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep9f .bs { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bep9f .bar { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .bep9f .bar.red { fill: var(--red); }
  .bep9f .bound { stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .bep9f figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
